cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Error Propagation in Cascaded Speech Translation under Acoustic Channel Degradations: A Black-Box Benchmark of Commercial Speech Intelligence APIs"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: CascadeBench Authors
    website: "https://github.com/43aquarius"
keywords:
  - speech recognition
  - speech translation
  - robustness benchmark
  - acoustic channel degradation
  - black-box API evaluation
  - error propagation
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/43aquarius/CascadeBench-Paper-AppliedAcoustics"
abstract: >-
  CascadeBench is a fully seeded, black-box benchmark measuring how twelve
  acoustic channel degradations propagate through commercial speech
  recognition and translation APIs: 480 bilingual sentences, six recognisers
  across three architectural families, four translation paths, and 26,238
  logged API calls on complimentary quotas.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
